            <div xml:id="d199">

                <pb facs="0370" n="271" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg271"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.11L5232/602: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Mayer</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-06-18T18:00:00-04:00">June 18, 1936—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>72. Department’s 70, June 16, 6 p.m. Department was informed on June 17 by a
                    representative of the German Embassy that he had been directed by the Ambassador
                    to say that the German Agent for the Mixed Claims Commission had received from
                    the German Government, through the Foreign Office, an instruction to request the
                    postponement <pb facs="0371" n="272" xml:id="pg272"/> of the hearings in the
                    sabotage cases. The Ambassador thought that this fact implied that the German
                    Government is willing to enter into negotiations concerning the subject matter
                    before the Commission, and he felt certain that the representatives of this
                    Government would be welcomed by the Foreign Office and other offices of the
                    German Government. He did not consider that explicit instructions from Berlin
                    were required.</p>
                <p>The Department is arranging to send representatives and will later advise you
                    more specifically.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
